<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss state dept official to visit The Hague.</title>
<headline>Swiss state dept official to visit The Hague.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss Federal Department of Foreign Affairs said Monday one of its top-ranking officials would visit his Dutch counterpart in The Hague on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Netherlands took over the presidency of the European Union at the start of this year.</p>
<p>Jakob Kellenberger, state secretary in the Swiss Department, will visit Michiel Patijn to discuss European integration and security matters, as well as the situation in ex-Yugoslavia and in Russia, the peace process in Middle East and Swiss bilateral relations, the Department said.</p>
</text>
